== A  Euler-Lagrange derivation and the meaning of F(0)
PASS A1 EL equation of L = -(a0^2/8piG)F(y) - rho*phi is div(F'(y) grad phi) = 4 pi G rho (mu = F')
PASS A2 MUTATION: prefactor 1/(4 pi G) does not give div(mu grad phi) = 4 pi G rho
PASS A3 F = y reproduces Poisson  lap(phi) = 4 pi G rho
PASS A4 additive constant of F is invisible to the field equation (the 'offset' is fixed only by the normalisation choice)
PASS A5 F(0) = int_0^inf (1-mu) dy evaluated symbolically for mu = 1-e^{-x}: c = 2
PASS A6 a constant L = -rho_off has T_00 = +rho_off, T_ii = -rho_off (a cosmological term, w = -1) from the metric variation of sqrt(-g) L (Minkowski point)

== B  c = int (1-mu) dy = int x^2 dmu  (second moment of the transition)
