PASS B1 c = int(1-mu)dy equals the second moment int x^2 mu'(x) dx for 5 families (integration by parts, boundary term x^2(1-mu) -> 0)
PASS B2 MUTATION: the FIRST moment int(1-mu)dx (= 1 for the exponential) is not c (= 2): the weight 2x matters

== C  lower bound c >= 1/3 when mu' <= mu'(0) = 1 (density of the CDF is bounded by its value at 0)
   random monotone-density search: min c = 0.333333 (bathtub value 1/3 = 0.333333); sharp transition c = 0.333333
PASS C1 for 20000 random nonincreasing densities with f(0)=1: c >= 1/3 (sharp transition attains it)
PASS C2 CONTROL: with mu' > mu'(0) allowed (non-concave mu) c = 0.0174 < 1/3, so the bound really needs mu' <= 1
PASS C3 no upper bound: c[mu] over concave mu is unbounded (mu_n, n -> 2+, has c ~ 1/(n-2)): c(2.001) = 999.694

== D  when is c finite?  tail 1-mu ~ A x^-p
   partial c(X) for X = 1e2..1e8:
   simple (p=1)         190.77     1986.18     19981.6    199977.0  1.99997e+6      2.0e+7      2.0e+8
   standard (p=2)      4.79835      7.1009     9.40349     11.7061     14.0087     16.3112     18.6138
   T-excess (p=1)      98.3771     997.801     9997.23     99996.7    999996.0      1.0e+7      1.0e+8
PASS D1 partial c for the simple mu = 2X - 2 ln(1+X) (linear divergence) [closed form vs quadrature at X=1e2..1e8]
PASS D2 partial c for the standard mu = asinh X + X^2 - X sqrt(1+X^2) ~ ln(2X) - 1/2 (log divergence) [closed form vs quadrature]
PASS D3 Milgrom-1999 temperature-excess form 1-mu ~ 1/(2x): partial c grows like X (linear divergence): c(1e8)/c(1e6) = 100.0
   Milgrom mu_n, c(n) closed form vs quadrature (log-variable x = e^u so that slow tails are resolved):
   n =  2.05: quad    19.7234861206   closed    19.7234861206
   n =   2.5: quad    1.90030027798   closed    1.90030027798
   n =     3: quad              1.0   closed              1.0
   n =     4: quad   0.599070117368   closed   0.599070117368
   n =     6: quad   0.431184926538   closed   0.431184926538
   n =    10: quad   0.366097722989   closed   0.366097722989
PASS D4 mu_n: c(n) = -(2/n) Gamma(3/n) Gamma(-2/n)/Gamma(1/n) (finite n > 2) matches numerical integration for n = 2.05...10
PASS D5 c(n) = 1 at n=3 and c(n) ~ 1/(n-2) as n -> 2+ (c(2.001)*(0.001) = 0.999694)
PASS D6 MUTATION: the naive sign (+(2/n)Gamma(3/n)Gamma(-2/n)/Gamma(1/n)) is negative for n>2 and is rejected by the numerics
PASS D7 synthetic tail (1+x)^-p: p = 2.5 gives finite c = 2/((p-1)(p-2)) = 2.6666667 (quad 2.6666667)
PASS D8 p = 1.5: partial c grows as X^(1/2) (x10 per two decades): ratios ['10.18', '10.02']

== E  c for the standard families
   sharp min(x,1)                                           c =   0.3333333333   G rho/a0^2 = c/(8 pi) = 0.0132629
   exponential 1-e^-x                                       c =            2.0   G rho/a0^2 = c/(8 pi) = 0.0795775
   Milgrom mu_n, n=3                                        c =            1.0   G rho/a0^2 = c/(8 pi) = 0.0397887
