   Milgrom mu_n, n=6                                        c =   0.4311849265   G rho/a0^2 = c/(8 pi) = 0.0171563
   Milgrom mu_n, n=10                                       c =    0.366097723   G rho/a0^2 = c/(8 pi) = 0.0145666
   RAR-nu (proper AQUAL inverse)                            c =    25.97575761   G rho/a0^2 = c/(8 pi) = 1.03354
   RAR mu=1-e^-sqrt(x) at g_obs (wrong deep-MOND limit)     c =           24.0   G rho/a0^2 = c/(8 pi) = 0.95493
   record OR family (1+x/N)^-N, N=3                         c =            9.0   G rho/a0^2 = c/(8 pi) = 0.358099
   record OR family (1+x/N)^-N, N=5                         c =    4.166666667   G rho/a0^2 = c/(8 pi) = 0.165786
   (RAR-nu second method (scipy, inverse by brentq): 25.975757606)
PASS E1 sharp transition c = 1/3 exactly, exponential c = 2 exactly
PASS E2 RAR-nu (proper inverse): two independent integrations agree: 25.9757576 vs 25.9757576 (lane G: 25.976)
PASS E3 the literal-argument reading mu(x) = 1 - e^{-sqrt x} gives exactly c = 24 (but its deep limit mu ~ sqrt(x) is NOT deep-MOND: excluded as a MOND mu)
PASS E4 literal reading: mu/x -> infinity as x -> 0 (mu ~ sqrt(x)); a MOND mu must have mu/x -> 1
PASS E5 OR family closed forms: c(N) = 2N^2/((N-1)(N-2)) [(1+x/N)^-N] verified vs quadrature at N = 3, 5
PASS E6 OR family literal-compact reading (p = min(g/s,1), mu = 1-(1-g/s)^N on g<s): c = 2N^2/((N+1)(N+2)) < 2 for every N (verified at N=2: 0.66666667 vs quad 0.66666667)
PASS E7 the record's own N = 2 shape (kappa = 1/2) is the MARGINAL member: 1-mu = 4/(2+x)^2 ~ 4/x^2, c(X) = 8[ln(1+X/2) + 2/(2+X) - 1] -> infinity (closed form vs quadrature at X = 1e3, 1e6)
PASS E8 tail amplitudes: standard 1-mu -> 1/(2x^2); record N=2 -> 4/x^2 (8x heavier); simple -> 1/x; T-excess -> 1/(2x)

